2026-08-01T22:20+0200 student unify-text-first-frame-and-icon-vocabulary §5.1 — the grid basis stopped being a constant and became a value. AppLayoutTheme is a ThemeExtension carrying the five numbers the whole grid resolves to (gutter, baseline, blockGrid, rowHeight, headerHeight), defaulting to the AppLayout constants; AppLayout.of(context) reads the basis in force and falls back to the constants when no extension is registered, so a bare-MaterialApp widget test still measures the shipped frame and nothing had to be wired for existing tests to keep passing. Registered once in ThemeData.extensions; AppScreen (header height, content/pinned/header gutters), AppRow (min height) and the eight screens that pad their own content band now read it, so a subtree wrapped in a Theme re-flows on the next frame with no hot restart — which is exactly what 5.3's sliders need and why 5.1 comes first. Proved red-first: the override case measured the default 24pt gutter (and the clamp's centring, which is why the assertion computes the column edge rather than asserting the gutter alone) until the frame stopped reading the constant. Also pushed the drill commit, which needed a rebase — the release bot had cut v1.8.0 on top. GATE: analyze 0 errors / 0 warnings, 1404 pass / 3 skip / 0 fail; docs ledger red on 08/11 from the release bump + ROADMAP, restamped in the follow-up commit per the lag rule. NOT PROVEN: how any basis other than the default looks (no gallery until 5.2, and looking is owner-gated anyway); the four AppLayout constants that are NOT in the extension (contentTopGap, sectionGap, itemGap, cardPadding) still ignore an override, which is a deliberate line — five numbers, not fifteen — but means a slider on blockGrid will not move the section rhythm.
